~ enter_door
Go inside?
- Enter
	$> go_to_room()
	=> END
- Nevermind
=> END

~ dumpster
You: Yes. [wait="ui_accept"]This is a dumpster.
- Jump inside
	You: ...Not doing that.
	=> END
- Nevermind
	=> END
	
# At the start of the game before anything else, you wake up in a dumpster and in your hungover haze,
# you have no clue why you were here
~ wake_up
You: I came here... [wait=1] for a reason... [wait=2] which was to...
	

#This is when Ollie throws the newspaper
~ newspaper_smack
You: Hey what the hell!
Boy on Bike: Read it dummy!
# ANIMATION: Show headline of newspaper, mentioning the murder you're here to investigate
You: What ever happened to basic human decency- 
You: Oh ya, that's why I'm here.
# ANIMATION: return to normal view

# If you chose to talk to the super who's working outside
~ super_outside
Super: Never thought something like this could happen in [i]my[/i] building.
You: It's a doggy dog world out there.
Super: What?
You: It's a doggy dog world out there.
Super: You mean dog eat dog?
You: Why would they do that? That's disgusting.
Super: nevermind...
=> crime_scene_question

~ crime_scene_question
- Ask where the crime happened
	You: Where did the dogs eat the other dogs?
	Super: If you're talking about where the body was found, it's room 11, first floor on the left.
	# I set it up like this cuz so that the user can repeat dialogue
	# TODO: set a conditional so that dialogue goes straight to here if you re-interact? 
	=> crime_scene_question 
- Leave
	=> END